"messages":[{"content":"Solve the problem step by step. Give your final answer in \\boxed{...}.\n\nThere exist constants $c_2,$ $c_1,$ and $c_0$ such that\n\\[x^3 + x^2 - 5 = (x - 3)^3 + c_2 (x - 3)^2 + c_1 (x - 3) + c_0.\\]Find $c_2^2 + c_1^2 + c_0^2.$","role":"user"}],"rendered_sha256":"461bdd88a6b14346e3bb9b0a0dd1ab15e81edab6484ecd77a1dde789df9ef4aa"},"seconds":56.04840302467346,"seed":894319515744446808,"stop":"eos","text":"To solve for the constants \\(c_2\\), \\(c_1\\), and \\(c_0\\) in the equation \n\\[x^3 + x^2 - 5 = (x - 3)^3 + c_2 (x - 3)^2 + c_1 (x - 3) + c_0,\\]\nwe first expand the right-hand side in terms of \\(x\\).\n\n1. **Expand \\((x - 3)^3\\):**\n   \\[\n   (x - 3)^3 = x^3 - 9x^2 + 27x - 27.\n   \\]\n\n2. **Expand \\(c_2 (x - 3)^2\\):**\n   \\[\n   c_2 (x - 3)^2 = c_2 (x^2 - 6x + 9) = c_2 x^2 - 6c_2 x + 9c_2.\n   \\]\n\n3. **Expand \\(c_1 (x - 3)\\):**\n   \\[\n   c_1 (x - 3) = c_1 x - 3c_1.\n   \\]\n\n4. **Combine all terms:**\n   \\[\n   (x - 3)^3 + c_2 (x - 3)^2 + c_1 (x - 3) + c_0 = x^3 - 9x^2 + 27x - 27 + c_2 x^2 - 6c_2 x + 9c_2 + c_1 x - 3c_1 + c_0.\n   \\]\n\n5. **Group the terms by powers of \\(x\\):**\n   \\[\n   x^3 + (-9 + c_2)x^2 + (27 - 6c_2 + c_1)x + (-27 + 9c_2 - 3c_1 + c_0).\n   \\]\n\nWe now equate the coefficients of the expanded form to the original polynomial \\(x^3 + x^2 - 5\\):\n\n- Coefficient of \\(x^3\\): \\(1 = 1\\)\n- Coefficient of \\(x^2\\): \\(-9 + c_2 = 1\\)\n- Coefficient of \\(x\\): \\(27 - 6c_2 + c_1 = 0\\)\n- Constant term: \\(-27 + 9c_2 - 3c_1 + c_0 = -5\\)\n\n6. **Solve for \\(c_2\\):**\n   \\[\n   -9 + c_2 = 1 \\implies c_2 = 10.\n   \\]\n\n7. **Solve for \\(c_1\\):**\n   \\[\n   27 - 6c_2 + c_1 = 0 \\implies 27 - 6(10) + c_1 = 0 \\implies 27 - 60 + c_1 = 0 \\implies c_1 = 33.\n   \\]\n\n8. **Solve for \\(c_0\\):**\n   \\[\n   -27 + 9c_2 - 3c_1 + c_0 = -5 \\implies -27 + 9(10) - 3(33) + c_0 = -5 \\implies -27 + 90 - 99 + c_0 = -5 \\implies -36 + c_0 = -5 \\implies c_0 = 31.\n   \\]\n\n9. **Calculate \\(c_2^2 + c_1^2 + c_0^2\\):**\n   \\[\n   c_2^2 + c_1^2 + c_0^2 = 10^2 + 33^2 + 31^2 = 100 + 1089 + 961 = 2150.\n   \\]\n\nThus, the final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{2150}\n\\]"},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{2150}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true}}
